 *  inertia). See briefs/04_sentinel_hunter_curiosity.md.
 *  Scope: section 11 build leash step 4.
 *  Authority: SIRENS_SONG_SPEC.md > agent.md > briefs/04_sentinel_hunter_curiosity.md
 *
 *  Invariants (CGI agent.md section 2):
 *   - INV1 No enemy HP / no player kill-path: HELD. Photos don't damage
 *     anything. Drones cannot harm the Patroller. No new kill paths.
 *   - INV2 Suspicion is the spine: EXTENDED. Drone-photo +15 and
 *     factory-proximity +1..+3/sec both wired through applySuspicion or
 *     the continuous-decay block. No scripted aggression added.
 *   - INV3 Perceiving costs: HELD AND EXTENDED. Drone deploy/move free
 *     (per spec section 3 table); drone PHOTO costs +15. Sub-cam photo
 *     no flat cost; the proximity to factory drives the cost (spec
 *     section 6). Passive sonar remains the only consistently free
 *     reveal.
 *   - INV4 Tools buy time / cost heat: n/a yet (step 5). Drones are
 *     perception platforms in step 3 (Scout + Photograph functions
 *     only; Decoy is step 4).
 *   - INV5 Fairness valve: PRESERVED. Step 2's instakill-sustain logic
 *     unchanged. Factory proximity only adds gain; never bypasses the
 *     warning window. Decay/valve relationship intact.
 *   - INV6 Function before form: HELD. Sentinel + Hunter = labeled
 *     placeholder circles with type-distinguishing color hint. Decoy
 *     mode = additional ring around drone (placeholder, NOT a form pass).
 *     Factory = labeled rectangle; objectives = labeled markers; drones
 *     = small circles with id; extraction = labeled corner rect. No
 *     palette/sound/sprite; color hints are testing legibility aids.
 *
 *  Step 4 additions (per brief 04):
 *   - Sentinel: orbits the power-core objective at small radius; large
 *     detection radius; suspicion contributes via proximity; rams at
 *     Alert+ (same as Patroller).
 *   - Hunter: dormant below Alert (no movement); at Alert+ pursues
 *     last-known sub/ping at speed; rams at Alert+; LOS-gated visibility.
 *   - Curiosity (cross-cutting all 3 Sirens): in Curious state, any
 *     Siren moves slowly to investigate the nearest valid decoy or the
 *     last ping origin (whichever is closer + visible). Non-lethal
 *     speed; does NOT damage drones at Curious.
 *   - Decoy drones (per Pat 2026-06-03 ruling): BOTH passive (any
 *     parked drone draws Curious Sirens) AND active (toggle "B" on a
 *     drone for stronger draw via larger effective radius). Documented
 *     in code comments; both routes implemented.
 *   - Siren-near-sub suspicion (+scaling/sec, spec section 6): summed
 *     over all Sirens within their per-type proximity range, distance-
 *     scaled. Folded into the same netRate block as factory proximity.
 *
 *  Step scope per brief 04:
 *    DO:    Sentinel + Hunter; curiosity behavior for all 3 Siren types;
 *           decoy mode on drones (passive + active); Siren-near-sub
 *           suspicion contribution; LOS-gated visibility for new Sirens.
 *    DON'T: Disruption tools (step 5); recon (step 6); final tuning
 *           pass (step 7); new objectives or new win/lose conditions.
 * ========================================================================= */

const canvas = document.getElementById("game");
const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
const hud = document.getElementById("hud");

const WORLD_W = canvas.width;
const WORLD_H = canvas.height;

/* ----- Tuning -------------------------------------------------------- */
const TUNING = {
  // step 1 (substrate)
  HULL_MAX: 3,
  OXYGEN_MAX_SECONDS: 240,
  // SUB_SPEED_PX_PER_SEC stays as the TERMINAL max linear speed cap.
  // (Step 1 fix-pass 2026-06-04 re-meaning: previously this was the
  // direct velocity when thrust was held; now it is the speed the sub
  // asymptotes to under continuous thrust, with acceleration to get
  // there and drag to bleed off.)
  SUB_SPEED_PX_PER_SEC: 80,
  // SUB_TURN_RATE_RAD_PER_SEC stays as the TERMINAL max angular speed cap.
